From: Brian.Hawthorne@East.Sun.COM (Brian Holt Hawthorne - SunSelect Engineering)
Subject: HEX: money supply

Derek makes some good points, which basically boil down to the
fact that the small number of Thornes and the fact that they
are indivisible makes for a money supply that is too small.

This lack of liquidity is keeping the wheels of the exchange from
turning smoothly.

I have taken the interim step of distributing additional shares of
HEX, which will have the effect of getting more of the money supply
out of HEX's coffers and into everyone else's.

If this is insufficient, I may take Derek's suggestion, and basically
do a 100 for 1 split on Thornes. This will not be the same as simply
printing additional money, since everyone's Thornes will be multplied
by 100. In other words, Thornes will be worth 1% of what they were
before, but everyone will have 100 times as many of them.

If I do this, all outstanding orders will be cancelled, and the
"Last Trade" price for each reputation will be set to 1% of its 
current price (or p1, whichever is more).

Any HEX traders who have comments one way or another on this should be
sure to post them (or send email to hex-comments@sea.east.sun.com).

